---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import BoneFiltrationDemo from '../../components/BoneFiltrationDemo.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Topology and Bone Fragility"
  description="An interactive introduction to John Rick Manzanares's research on topology, morphometry, and trabecular bone structure."
>
  <header class="research-hero" id="question">
    <div class="shell research-hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">Doctoral research · Interactive explanation</p>
        <h1>Can shape help explain bone strength?</h1>
        <p class="research-lead">
          Trabecular bone is not simply more bone or less bone. It is a network in three dimensions.
          Connectivity, tunnels, cavities, orientation, local geometry, and load paths all contribute
          to its architecture.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <a class="button" href="#explore">Explore the topology</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="#pipeline">See the research pipeline</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="research-question" aria-label="Central research question">
        <p class="eyebrow">Central question</p>
        <p>
          Can topological descriptors capture aspects of trabecular architecture that complement
          conventional morphometry when apparent bone strength is the outcome of interest?
        </p>
        <div class="question-chain" aria-label="Research sequence">
          <span>micro CT</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span>structure</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span>topology</span>
          <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          <span>strength</span>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </header>

  <nav class="research-local-nav" aria-label="On this research page">
    <div class="shell">
      <a href="#question">Question</a>
      <a href="#explore">Explore</a>
      <a href="#depth">Read deeper</a>
      <a href="#pipeline">Pipeline</a>
      <a href="#evidence">Evidence</a>
      <a href="#next">Next questions</a>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <section class="section section-soft">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="research-disclosure">
        <article>
          <p class="eyebrow">What this page does</p>
          <h2>It explains the research idea in layers.</h2>
          <p>
            The page begins with intuition, then connects a synthetic filtration to persistence,
            introduces the mathematical structure, and finally shows how the ideas enter the research workflow.
          </p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <p class="eyebrow">What this page does not do</p>
          <h2>It does not present unpublished outcome results.</h2>
          <p>
            No research specimen images, identifying information, or detailed numerical results from the
            manuscript are shown in the teaching interaction.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="explore">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Start with the idea</p>
          <h2>Topology asks a different structural question.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Conventional morphometry measures quantities such as bone volume fraction, trabecular thickness,
          separation, connectivity density, and anisotropy. Persistent homology studies how topological
          features appear and disappear across a changing threshold or scalar field.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="dimension-grid">
        <article>
          <span class="dimension">H<sub>0</sub></span>
          <h3>Components</h3>
          <p>Tracks separate pieces and the thresholds at which they merge.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="dimension">H<sub>1</sub></span>
          <h3>Tunnels</h3>
          <p>Tracks loop structure surrounding a passage that has not been filled.</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <span class="dimension">H<sub>2</sub></span>
          <h3>Cavities</h3>
          <p>Tracks voids enclosed by surrounding structure in three dimensions.</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <BoneFiltrationDemo />

      <div class="bridge-block">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">From the teaching example to the research data</p>
          <h2>The object changes, but the logic is the same.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="bridge-grid">
          <article>
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>Start with an image volume</h3>
            <p>A calibrated micro CT volume provides intensity and spatial information inside a defined analysis region.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>Build a scalar filtration</h3>
            <p>Image intensity or signed distance values determine when cells enter a cubical complex.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>Track topology across thresholds</h3>
            <p>Persistent homology records which structural features survive as the filtration changes.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section depth-section" id="depth">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Read at the level you need</p>
          <h2>One project, three ways in.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          The scientific question is the same in every view. Only the level of detail changes.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="depth-interface" data-depth-interface>
        <div class="depth-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Explanation level">
          <button
            id="tab-intuition"
            type="button"
            role="tab"
            aria-selected="true"
            aria-controls="panel-intuition"
            data-depth-tab="intuition"
          >
            Intuition
          </button>
          <button
            id="tab-mathematics"
            type="button"
            role="tab"
            aria-selected="false"
            aria-controls="panel-mathematics"
            data-depth-tab="mathematics"
          >
            Mathematics
          </button>
          <button
            id="tab-implementation"
            type="button"
            role="tab"
            aria-selected="false"
            aria-controls="panel-implementation"
            data-depth-tab="implementation"
          >
            Implementation
          </button>
        </div>

        <div class="depth-panels">
          <section
            id="panel-intuition"
            role="tabpanel"
            aria-labelledby="tab-intuition"
            data-depth-panel="intuition"
          >
            <p class="eyebrow">Intuition</p>
            <h3>A single threshold can hide how structure changes.</h3>
            <p>
              A binary segmentation gives one answer at one chosen threshold. Persistent homology instead
              studies a sequence of related shapes. A feature that disappears almost immediately behaves
              differently from one that remains present across a broad part of the filtration.
            </p>
            <p>
              Persistence is therefore about stability across change. The aim in this project is not to
              replace morphometry, but to ask whether topology provides complementary information about architecture.
            </p>
          </section>

          <section
            id="panel-mathematics"
            role="tabpanel"
            aria-labelledby="tab-mathematics"
            data-depth-panel="mathematics"
          >
            <p class="eyebrow">Mathematics</p>
            <h3>A filtration is a nested family of complexes.</h3>
            <p>
              Let <em>K</em> be a cubical complex and let <em>f</em> assign a scalar filtration value to its cells.
              For a threshold <em>t</em>, define the sublevel complex
            </p>

            <div class="math-display" aria-label="K sub t equals the set of cells Q such that f of Q is less than or equal to t">
              <math display="block">
                <msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub>
                <mo>=</mo>
                <mo>{</mo>
                <mi>Q</mi>
                <mo>:</mo>
                <mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo>)</mo>
                <mo>≤</mo>
                <mi>t</mi>
                <mo>}</mo>
                <mo>.</mo>
              </math>
            </div>

            <p>
              If <em>s</em> is at most <em>t</em>, then <em>K</em><sub>s</sub> is contained in
              <em>K</em><sub>t</sub>. Inclusion induces a map on homology:
            </p>

            <div class="math-display" aria-label="H k of K sub s maps to H k of K sub t">
              <math display="block">
                <msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub>
                <mo>(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>)</mo>
                <mo>→</mo>
                <msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub>
                <mo>(</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>)</mo>
                <mo>.</mo>
              </math>
            </div>

            <p>
              Persistent homology records when homology classes appear and when they disappear.
              A finite class can be represented by a point <span class="nowrap">(birth, death)</span>
              in a persistence diagram. The difference between death and birth is its persistence.
            </p>

            <aside class="math-note">
              <strong>Important distinction.</strong>
              A persistence class is algebraic. A geometric cycle used to illustrate it is a representative,
              and representatives need not be unique.
            </aside>
          </section>

          <section
            id="panel-implementation"
            role="tabpanel"
            aria-labelledby="tab-implementation"
            data-depth-panel="implementation"
          >
            <p class="eyebrow">Implementation</p>
            <h3>Images become scalar fields, then cubical filtrations.</h3>
            <p>
              Image volumes are restricted to an analysis region and converted into scalar filtrations based
              on quantities such as image intensity or signed distance. Cubical persistent homology then produces
              interval or diagram data that can be transformed into representations suitable for modelling.
            </p>
            <p>
              The conventional morphometry code is deliberately kept separate from the persistent homology workflow.
              The public <code>bone_morphometry</code> package handles morphometry and other scalar descriptors.
              Topological analysis remains independently inspectable in the associated research repository.
            </p>
            <div class="inline-links">
              <a href="https://github.com/jhnrckmnznrs/bone_morphometry" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">bone_morphometry →</a>
              <a href="https://github.com/jhnrckmnznrs/boneStrengthPrediction" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Topological analysis code →</a>
            </div>
          </section>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="pipeline">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Research provenance</p>
          <h2>Make the path from image to model visible.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Each stage changes the object being analysed. Showing those changes helps separate image processing,
          mathematical description, and statistical modelling.
        </p>
      </div>

      <ol class="pipeline">
        <li>
          <span>01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Image volume and analysis region</h3>
            <p>Begin with a calibrated volume and an explicitly defined region of interest.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Preprocessing and segmentation</h3>
            <p>Construct a bone representation while preserving the intended analysis domain.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Scalar filtration</h3>
            <p>Use image intensity or distance information to determine when cells enter the complex.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>04</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Persistent homology</h3>
            <p>Track topological classes in dimensions 0, 1, and 2 across the filtration.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>05</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Numerical representation</h3>
            <p>Transform persistence information into features that can be compared or used in statistical models.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span>06</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Validation and strength modelling</h3>
            <p>Compare topological and morphometric feature families with procedures appropriate for a small cohort.</p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-soft" id="evidence">
    <div class="shell evidence-grid">
      <article class="evidence-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Public now</p>
        <h2>Methods, software, and the conceptual interface</h2>
        <p>
          The mathematical idea, the teaching interaction, and public software can be inspected without
          releasing detailed outcome comparisons before the corresponding manuscript is public.
        </p>
        <div class="inline-links">
          <a href="https://github.com/jhnrckmnznrs/bone_morphometry" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Inspect the Rust package →</a>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="evidence-card status-card">
        <p class="eyebrow">Still in preparation</p>
        <h2>Detailed numerical comparisons</h2>
        <p>
          Strength prediction tables, manuscript figures, and other detailed outcome results are intentionally
          absent from this public teaching page for now.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section next-questions" id="next">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="kicker">Questions that follow</p>
          <h2>The first descriptor is not the end of the problem.</h2>
        </div>
        <p>
          Bone structure also raises questions about direction, invariance, mechanics, and field learning.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="question-grid">
        <article>
          <h3>Direction</h3>
          <p>How should topology respond when trabecular architecture has a preferred orientation?</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Invariance</h3>
          <p>Which descriptors retain their meaning when the coordinate frame changes?</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Mechanics</h3>
          <p>How do structural changes relate to load paths, stiffness, and local weakness?</p>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Operator learning</h3>
          <p>Can topology help learned field models preserve information that matters to the physics?</p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="return-link">
        <a class="text-link" href="/research/">← Back to all research</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    const interfaceRoot = document.querySelector('[data-depth-interface]');

    if (interfaceRoot) {
      const tabs = Array.from(interfaceRoot.querySelectorAll('[data-depth-tab]'));
      const panels = Array.from(interfaceRoot.querySelectorAll('[data-depth-panel]'));

      interfaceRoot.dataset.enhanced = 'true';

      const select = (name) => {
        tabs.forEach((tab) => {
          const selected = tab.dataset.depthTab === name;
          tab.setAttribute('aria-selected', String(selected));
          tab.tabIndex = selected ? 0 : -1;
        });

        panels.forEach((panel) => {
          panel.hidden = panel.dataset.depthPanel !== name;
        });
      };

      tabs.forEach((tab, index) => {
        tab.addEventListener('click', () => select(tab.dataset.depthTab));

        tab.addEventListener('keydown', (event) => {
          if (!['ArrowLeft', 'ArrowRight', 'Home', 'End'].includes(event.key)) return;

          event.preventDefault();
          let nextIndex = index;

          if (event.key === 'ArrowRight') nextIndex = (index + 1) % tabs.length;
          if (event.key === 'ArrowLeft') nextIndex = (index - 1 + tabs.length) % tabs.length;
          if (event.key === 'Home') nextIndex = 0;
          if (event.key === 'End') nextIndex = tabs.length - 1;

          tabs[nextIndex].focus();
          select(tabs[nextIndex].dataset.depthTab);
        });
      });

      select('intuition');
    }
  </script>

  <style>
    .research-hero {
      padding: clamp(4.5rem, 9vw, 8rem) 0 4rem;
    }

    .research-hero-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.15fr) minmax(320px, .85fr);
      gap: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 6rem);
      align-items: end;
    }

    .research-hero h1 {
      margin: 0;
      max-width: 13ch;
      font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
      font-size: clamp(3.2rem, 7.2vw, 6.6rem);
      font-weight: 500;
      line-height: .95;
      letter-spacing: -.052em;
    }

    .research-lead {
      max-width: 720px;
      margin: 1.5rem 0 0;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      font-size: clamp(1.08rem, 1.7vw, 1.3rem);
    }

    .research-question {
      padding: 1.5rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 26px;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,.45);
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
    }

    .research-question > p:not(.eyebrow) {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 1.45rem;
      line-height: 1.35;
    }

    .question-chain {
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: .45rem;
      align-items: center;
      margin-top: 1.25rem;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      font-size: .76rem;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: .08em;
    }

    .question-chain span:nth-child(even) { color: var(--terracotta); }

    .research-local-nav {
      position: sticky;
      top: 76px;
      z-index: 70;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      background: rgba(244,241,234,.94);
      backdrop-filter: blur(14px);
    }

    .research-local-nav .shell {
      display: flex;
      gap: .25rem;
      padding-block: .55rem;
      overflow-x: auto;
      scrollbar-width: thin;
    }

    .research-local-nav a {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      padding: .35rem .6rem;
      border-radius: 999px;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      text-decoration: none;
      font-size: .78rem;
    }

    .research-local-nav a:hover,
    .research-local-nav a:focus-visible {
      color: var(--ink);
      background: rgba(70,96,82,.08);
    }

    .research-disclosure {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .research-disclosure article {
      padding: clamp(1.2rem, 3vw, 2rem);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 20px;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,.34);
    }

    .research-disclosure h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 1.8rem;
      line-height: 1.15;
    }

    .research-disclosure p:last-child {
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      margin-bottom: 0;
    }

    .dimension-grid,
    .question-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .dimension-grid article,
    .question-grid article {
      padding: 1.4rem;
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 20px;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,.35);
    }

    .dimension {
      color: var(--terracotta);
      font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 1.35rem;
    }

    .dimension-grid h3,
    .question-grid h3 {
      margin: .45rem 0 .5rem;
      font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 1.35rem;
    }

    .dimension-grid p,
    .question-grid p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
    }

    .bridge-block {
      margin-top: 3rem;
      padding-top: 2.5rem;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .bridge-block > div:first-child {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr;
      gap: 2rem;
      align-items: end;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }

    .bridge-block h2 {
      margin: 0;
      max-width: 12ch;
      font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.4rem);
      font-weight: 500;
      line-height: 1;
      letter-spacing: -.035em;
    }

    .bridge-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .bridge-grid article {
      padding: 1.2rem;
      border-top: 2px solid var(--pine);
      background: rgba(255,255,255,.25);
    }

    .bridge-grid span {
      color: var(--terracotta);
      font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
    }

    .bridge-grid h3 {
      margin: .5rem 0;
      font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
    }

    .bridge-grid p {
      margin: 0;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
    }

    .depth-section {
      background: rgba(70,96,82,.045);
    }

    .depth-interface {
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 24px;
      overflow: hidden;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,.4);
    }

    .depth-tabs {
      display: flex;
      gap: .35rem;
      padding: .6rem;
      border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
      overflow-x: auto;
    }

    .depth-tabs button {
      appearance: none;
      border: 0;
      border-radius: 999px;
      padding: .65rem .9rem;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
      background: transparent;
      font: inherit;
      font-size: .88rem;
      font-weight: 750;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .depth-tabs button[aria-selected='true'] {
      color: var(--paper);
      background: var(--ink);
    }

    .depth-tabs button:focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--ochre);
      outline-offset: 2px;
    }

    .depth-panels {
      padding: clamp(1.4rem, 4vw, 2.5rem);
    }

    .depth-panels section {
      max-width: 800px;
    }

    .depth-panels h3 {
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
      font-size: clamp(1.8rem, 3vw, 2.7rem);
      line-height: 1.1;
    }

    .depth-panels p { color: var(--ink-soft); }

    .math-display {
      margin: 1.5rem 0;
      overflow-x: auto;
      padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
      border-left: 3px solid var(--terracotta);
      background: rgba(166,90,67,.06);
      font-size: 1.25rem;
    }

    .math-note {
      margin-top: 1.5rem;
      padding: 1rem 1.1rem;
      border: 1px solid rgba(197,164,93,.55);
      border-radius: 14px;
      background: rgba(197,164,93,.08);
      color: var(--ink-soft);
    }

    .math-note strong { color: var(--ink); }
    .nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }

    .pipeline {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      list-style: none;
    }

    .pipeline li {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: 76px 1fr;
      gap: 1.2rem;
      padding: 1.35rem 0;
      border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
    }

    .pipeline li:last-child { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }

    .pipeline > li > span {
      color: var(--terracotta);
      font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 1.35rem;
    }

    .pipeline h3 {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 1.45rem;
    }

    .pipeline p {
      margin: .35rem 0 0;
      color: var(--ink-soft);
    }

    .evidence-grid {
      display: grid;
      grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .evidence-card {
      padding: clamp(1.4rem, 3vw, 2rem);
      border: 1px solid var(--line);
      border-radius: 22px;
      background: rgba(255,255,255,.4);
    }

    .evidence-card h2 {
      margin: 0;
      font-family: ui-serif, Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 2rem;
      line-height: 1.12;
    }

    .evidence-card > p:not(.eyebrow) { color: var(--ink-soft); }

    .status-card {
      border-color: rgba(197,164,93,.55);
      background: rgba(197,164,93,.08);
    }

    .question-grid { grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); }
    .return-link { margin-top: 2rem; }

    @media (max-width: 900px) {
      .research-hero-grid,
      .research-disclosure,
      .evidence-grid,
      .bridge-block > div:first-child {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .dimension-grid,
      .bridge-grid {
        grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      }

      .question-grid {
        grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
      }
    }

    @media (max-width: 600px) {
